\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl180\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1\cf0 .  There is a green hill far away,
\par \pard\li225\sl180\slmult0  Outside a city wall,
\par Where the dear Lord was crucified,
\par Who died to save us all.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl180\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  We may not know, we cannot tell
\par \pard\li225\sl180\slmult0   What pains he had to bear;
\par  But we believe it was for us
\par  He hung and suffered there.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl180\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.   He died that we might be forgiven
\par \pard\li225\sl180\slmult0  He died to make us good,
\par \pard\li315\sl180\slmult0 That we might go at last to heaven,
\par Saved by his precious blood.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl180\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4.   There was no other good enough
\par \pard\li315\sl180\slmult0 To pay the price of sin;
\par He only could unlock the gate
\par Of heaven, and let us in.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl180\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.   Oh, dearly, dearly has he loved,
\par \pard\li315\sl180\slmult0 And we must love him too,
\par And trust in his redeeming blood,
\par \pard       And try his works to do.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

